WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.140
Configuration management appears in many cybersecurity frameworks and standards.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:19.480
Organizations commonly encounter configuration management expectations in NIST SP 800-53, RMF, FedRAMP, CIS Controls, CMMC, ISO 27001, and other governance programs.

3
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.800
Frameworks emphasize configuration management because controlled configurations reduce risk and support consistent operations.

4
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.380
They also create evidence that systems are being managed responsibly.

5
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.420
Compliance readiness depends on more than saying a process exists.

6
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:44.960
Teams need records such as baselines, change approvals, configuration reviews, exceptions, monitoring results, and remediation actions.

7
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.120
Strong configuration management helps organizations demonstrate operational discipline.

8
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.580
It connects technical reality to governance expectations in a way that reviewers and system owners can understand.
